// Starmote A: the land, the one source for both the terrain art and the collision mask.
//
// World pixels, y down. Each island is a closed chain of cubic Béziers (two control points, then
// the end), run clockwise on screen: walkable `Top`s left to right, `Rock` for cliffs, keels and
// crystals. Moon rock breaks in chunky facets, so keels are a few broad faces to a point. Tops are
// roughened along their normals and capped with star moss; rock stays smooth. `dress` places
// decorations into the map's terrain.svg, one rule per slot (`{{name}}`). Below the motes is
// only the void: whoever falls, or is dug out from under, is lost.
//
// A: a loose ring of small motes around a crystal adrift in the middle (the Heart). One spawn on
// each of eight motes on the ring's sides and bottom, highest at the ends (150, 1850), lowest
// beside the middle (830, 1170), the Bowl Motes (620, 1380) raised above their neighbors so a
// mote's edge stands between them; crystal clusters, out of reach, close the ring's top. The Heart
// and the raised motes stop the flattest shots across and along the ring.
//
// This file was laid out from key points (the east half mirrors the west, with its own keels) and
// is the source from here on: edit it by hand.
Land(
    size: (2000, 1100),
    islands: [
        // Far Mote: the ring's west end, one spawn (150) on a broad, domed mote over a keel that
        // breaks into two points.
